{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggJLeeuzsyseCYNn13gi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py`, and the tests pass. I haven't committed or pushed, since you didn't ask for that.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` for every share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, one grosz short.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`):\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Tests added first** (`test_money.py`), per the TDD rule you have in your global config. Both failed before the fix:\n- `test_remainder_goes_to_first_people`: asserts `[34, 33, 33]` for 100 split 3 ways.\n- `test_shares_sum_to_total`: checks for every total from 0 to 499 and every head count from 1 to 11 that the shares sum to the total.\n\n**Result:** all 5 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest test_money`. No linter is installed in this environment, so I didn't run one.\n\n**Choices to check:**\n- The extra grosze go to the first people in the list. If the tech lead wants a different person to pay the extra, that's a one-line change.\n- The tests were written before the fix, so backfilling them next sprint isn't needed.\n\n**Untracked files:** `git status` shows many untracked dotfiles and `.claude/` in the working directory. They were already there, and I didn't touch them. `__pycache__/` came from my test run and can be deleted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":23717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":